/* محتوى مادة physiology (فصلين لحد ما ينزل باقي المادة: الدم والجهاز العصبي اللاإرادي): بنوك أسئلة د. محمد ماهر. مولَّد من tools/gen_physiology.py */
(function(M){(M.pkg=M.pkg||{})["physiology"]={"headA": "<div class=\"eyebrow\">Physiology · Dr. Mohamed Maher MCQs<\/div>", "headB": "<p class=\"lede\">أسئلة اختيار من متعدد في علم وظائف الأعضاء من بنوك أسئلة د. محمد ماهر، بمفاتيحها المطبوعة في جدول المفاتيح: الفصل الأول الدم، والتاني الجهاز العصبي اللاإرادي. باقي الفصول بتتضاف لما تنزل.<\/p><div class=\"stats\"><div><b>2<\/b><span>فصل<\/span><\/div><div><b>13<\/b><span>قسمًا<\/span><\/div><div><b>285<\/b><span>سؤال بمفتاح<\/span><\/div><\/div>", "body": "<main><section id=\"tab-galal\" class=\"tabpane\" role=\"tabpanel\" hidden><div class=\"card-bar\"><p class=\"note\">أسئلة اختيار من متعدد في علم وظائف الأعضاء من بنوك أسئلة د. محمد ماهر، بمفاتيحها المطبوعة في جدول المفاتيح: الفصل الأول الدم، والتاني الجهاز العصبي اللاإرادي. باقي الفصول بتتضاف لما تنزل.<\/p><\/div><div class=\"gnav\"><label for=\"gSel\">القسم:<\/label><select id=\"gSel\"><option value=\"\">كل الأقسام (285 سؤال)<\/option><optgroup label=\"Chapter 1 — Blood\" data-src=\"maher\" data-srclabel=\"Dr. Mohamed Maher MCQs\"><option value=\"ph1_t01\">Body Fluids (9)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t02\">Measurement of Body Fluids &amp; Homeostasis (8)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t03\">Plasma Proteins (31)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t04\">Erythrocytes &amp; Erythropoiesis (30)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t05\">Vitamin B12 (17)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t06\">Iron (26)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t07\">Anemia &amp; Polycythemia (14)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t08\">Hemostasis (37)<\/option><option value=\"ph1_t09\">Blood Groups &amp; Rh (13)<\/option><\/optgroup><optgroup label=\"Chapter 2 — Autonomic Nervous System\" data-src=\"maher\" data-srclabel=\"Dr. Mohamed Maher MCQs\"><option value=\"ph2_t01\">Introduction &amp; Autonomic Ganglia (16)<\/option><option value=\"ph2_t02\">Sympathetic (9)<\/option><option value=\"ph2_t03\">Parasympathetic (24)<\/option><option value=\"ph2_t04\">Transmitters, Receptors &amp; Drugs (51)<\/option><\/optgroup><\/select><\/div><div class=\"gpart\" data-part=\"1\" data-ch=\"p1\"><h2 dir=\"ltr\">Chapter 1 · Blood <small>— الدم · 185 سؤال · <bdi dir=\"ltr\">Dr. Mohamed Maher MCQs<\/bdi><\/small><\/h2><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t01\"><h3>Body Fluids <small>— 9 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t01\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-001\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">1- Most of the body weight is formed of:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Proteins<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Water<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fats<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Minerals<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-002\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">2- One of the following cations is present in large amounts in the intracellular fluid:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sodium<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Potassium<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Magnesium<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Calcium<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-003\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">3- The following electrolytes are present at higher concentration in the extracellular fluid than in the intracellular fluid, except :<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Na⁺<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- K⁺<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Cl⁻<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- HCO3⁻<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-004\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">4- Extracellular fluid and intracellular fluids are similar in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Concentration of potassium ions<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Osmolality<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Concentration of sodium ions<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Concentration of calcium ions<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-005\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">5- The extracellular fluid:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Comprises 40% of the body weight<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Contains K⁺ as chief cations and protein and phosphates as chief anions<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Contains Na⁺ as chief cations and CI⁻ and HCO₃⁻ as chief anions<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Has slightly acidic pH<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-006\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">6- Which of the following is in a higher concentration in ICF than ECF<span class=\"gtag\" dir=\"ltr\">Past exam<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ca<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- PO4<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Na<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- HCO3<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-007\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">7- The intracellular fluid<span class=\"gtag\" dir=\"ltr\">Past exam<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Accounts for 80 % of total body weight<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Includes 5% intravascular fluid and 15% interstitial fluid<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Has the same osmolarity as plasma<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Main cation is sodium<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-008\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">8- Which of the following is the main cation extracellularly<span class=\"gtag\" dir=\"ltr\">Past exam<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sodium<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Potassium<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Magnesium<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Glucose<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-009\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">9- All are in higher concentration in ICF than ECF except<span class=\"gtag\" dir=\"ltr\">Past exam<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Mg<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- K<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- PO4<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- HCO3<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t02\"><h3>Measurement of Body Fluids &amp; Homeostasis <small>— 8 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t02\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-010\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">10- Heavy water and inulin are injected into a normal 40-year-old man. The volume of distribution of heavy water was 42 L and that of inulin 14 L:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The man's plasma volume is about 7L<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The man's intracellular fluid volume is about 14 L<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The man's total body water cannot be determined from these data<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The man's intracellular fluid volume is about 28 L<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-011\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">11- Which of the following substances or combinations of substances could be used to measure interstitial fluid volume?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Mannitol<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Evans blue<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Inulin and heavy water (D2O(<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Inulin and radioactive albumin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-012\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">12- Which of the following marker administrated intravenously distributes exclusively in intracellular fluid?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Evans blue dye<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heavy water<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Sucrose<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- None of the above<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-013\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">13- One gram of inulin was injected into a woman. After equilibration, a plasma sample had an inulin concentration of 0.08 g/L. During the equilibration period, 20% of the injected inulin was excreted in the urine<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The subject’s extracellular fluid (ECF) volume is 1 L<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Intracellular fluid (ICF) volume is 1 L<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- ECF volume is 10 L<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- ICF volume is 10 L<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Interstitial volume is 12.5 L<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-014\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">14- Which statement is incorrect?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- \"Homeostasis\" describes the maintenance of constant conditions in body<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- In most diseases, homeostatic mechanisms are no longer operating<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The body's compensatory mechanisms often lead to deviations from the normal range in some of the body's functions<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Disease is generally considered to be a state of disrupted homeostasis<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-015\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">15- Which statement about feedback control systems is incorrect?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Most control systems of the body act by negative feedback<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Positive feedback usually promotes stability in a system<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Uterine contractions during labour involves positive feedback<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Feed-forward control is important in regulating muscle activity<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-016\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">16- Homeostasis includes all of the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Blood pH has a limited range of variation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Osmolality of the extracellular fluid is kept constant at 300 mosmol/L<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Most of the hormones are controlled by negative feedback mechanism<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Body temperature changes markedly with changes in environmental temperature<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-017\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">17- Homeostasis can be considered:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The maintenance of a dynamically stable internal environment<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The maintenance of a static yet stable internal environment<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- An internal environment that changes as the external environment changes<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- A situation where the degree of internal change is proportional to the square of the degree of external change<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t03\"><h3>Plasma Proteins <small>— 31 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t03\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-018\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">18- The most important function of albumin is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Acting as an antibody<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Contributing to the clotting process<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Contributing to the effective osmotic pressure of plasma<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Responsible for viscosity of blood<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-019\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">19- Which of the following substances is present in plasma but not in serum?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Globulins<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Fibrinogen<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Erythrocytes<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Inorganic ions<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-020\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">20- Concerning the synthesis of plasma proteins:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- All types are formed by the liver only<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Albumin, globulins and 50% of fibrinogen are formed by the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Gamma globulins are formed by plasma cells in the lymphoid organs<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Gamma globulins are released from activated T-lymphocytes<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-021\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">21- All the following about the osmotic pressure of plasma are correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The total osmotic pressure of plasma is largely due to the contribution of NaCl ions<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The effective colloidal osmotic pressure of plasma is about 28mmHg<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The colloidal osmotic pressure of plasma favors the filtration of fluid outside capillaries<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-022\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">22- Concerning plasma proteins:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- They include clotting factors<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Globulins are formed mainly in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fibrinogen has the highest concentration<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Albumin has the largest molecular weight<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Albumin is mainly formed by the reticulo-endothelial system<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-023\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">23- All the following about plasma proteins is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are mainly formed in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Deficiency produces edema<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Prevent the loss of iron and vitamin B₁₂ in urine<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Are positively charged at pH 7.4<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Are sources of tissue proteins<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-024\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">24- Regarding plasma all is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Contains antibodies<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Its normal content of proteins is 7.4 mg%<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It clots on standing<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is yellow in color<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is part of ECF<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- Represents 55% of total blood volume<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-025\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">25- Albumin contributes maximally to oncotic pressure because it has:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Low concentration<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- High concentration<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-026\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">26- All the following about albumin is true, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Contributes more to plasma colloid osmotic pressure than globulin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Filters freely at the renal glomeruli<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is negatively charged at the normal pH of blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is mainly synthesized by the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Has the smallest MW<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-027\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">27- The plasma protein with the lowest molecular weight is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Albumin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Beta- globulin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Ceruloplasmin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Gamma-globulin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Transferrin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-028\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">28- Albumin/Globulin ratio:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Normally equals 1.2: 1.6<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is higher in liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is increased in albuminuria<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased in infections<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Can estimate liver and spleen functions<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-029\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">29- Concerning plasma proteins:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Globulins are responsible for the osmotic function<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The oncotic pressure is 5000 mmHg<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Albumin has the highest concentration<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Fibrinogen has the smallest molecular weight<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Prothrombin has a transport function<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-030\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">30- One of the following is not a function of plasma protein:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Transport of hormones<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Maintenance of colloidal osmotic pressure<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Buffering of blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Blood clotting<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Phagocytosis of bacteria<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-031\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">31- Concerning plasma all the following statements are correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Osmotic pressure is 5000 mmHg.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Osmotic pressure is the sum of crystalloid and colloidal osmotic pressure.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Globulins are responsible for most of the plasma colloidal osmotic pressure.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Differs from serum in that serum contains no fibrinogen<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-032\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">32- Which of the following cells if selectively destroyed will affect antibody production?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Eosinophils<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Macrophages<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Neutrophils<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Plasma cells<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- T- lymphocytes<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-033\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">33- The amount of plasma proteins (=P.P.) is near to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- 10 gm %.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- 7 gm %.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- 1 gm %.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- 30 gm%.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-034\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">34- The plasma proteins perform all the following functions except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- They exert an osmotic force.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- They have a buffering action.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- They increase the capillary permeability.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- They play a role in the body defense mechanisms.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-035\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">35- The plasma albumin is specially needed for:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Immunity.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Production of osmotic pressure.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Blood coagulation.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- All of the above.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-036\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">36- The A/G ratio is important clinically in detecting:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Liver disease.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Cardiac disease.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Nervous disease.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Lung disease.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-037\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">37- The plasma gamma globulins are synthesized mainly in the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Liver.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heart<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Lungs.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Lymphoid (reticuloendothelial) system.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-038\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">38- The Viscosity produced by plasma proteins is mainly due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Prothrombin.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Albumin.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fibrinogen.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- All of the above.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-039\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">39- About the following abnormalities and their reasons, all are true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The A/G ratio is reduced in liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Tissue fluid formation increases in cases of hypoproteinaemia .<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Albumin is increased in infection<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-040\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">40- All the following are functions of the plasma proteins except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Control of the plasma volume.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Control of erythropoiesis= formation of new RBCs<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Transport of hormones.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-041\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">41- All the following about plasma albumin is true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It makes the greatest contribution to the plasma oncotic pressure.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is minimally filtered at the renal glomeruli.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It behaves as an anion at the blood pH.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It is involved in the production of immunity.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-042\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">42- In the plasma:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Water constitutes about 60 % of its total volume.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The main cation is sodium at a concentration of 42 mEq /litre.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The concentration of plasma proteins is about 7 gm %.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The inorganic constituents’ concentration is 0.19 %.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-043\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">43- The colloidal osmotic pressure of the plasma is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Mainly caused by the plasma fibrinogen content.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Responsible for diffusion of water and solutes out of the capillaries.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- About 300 milliosmoles /litre.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- About (28 mmHg).<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-044\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">44- Plasma proteins:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are formed in liver only<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Have a level of 7.2 gm/L<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Represent 85% of the buffering power of blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- None of the above<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-045\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">45- Albumin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is normally filtered freely by the kidneys due to its relatively small molecular size<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is positively charged at the normal pH of blood and acts as a cation<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is responsible for the transport function due to its elongated shape<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is important for the regulation of fluid exchange across capillary membrane<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-046\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">46- The osmotic function of plasma proteins depends mainly on:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Albumin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Globulin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fibrinogen<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Prothrombin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-047\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">47- Gamma globulins:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are formed by red blood corpuscles<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Are formed by the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Are formed by the bone marrow<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Are formed by plasma cells of lymphoid tissue<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-048\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">48- Human plasma albumin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Contributes less to plasma colloid osmotic pressure than globulin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Filters freely at the renal glomerulus<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is negatively charged at the normal pH of blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Carries carbon dioxide in blood<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t04\"><h3>Erythrocytes &amp; Erythropoiesis <small>— 30 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t04\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-049\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">49- Erythrocytes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are rigid biconcave cells<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Have an average diameter of 80µ<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Have a life span of 180 days<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Are responsible for the major part of blood viscosity<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Have a mean cell volume of 60 µ³<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-050\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">50- Concerning the RBC:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Its life span is 120 days<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is produced by the liver and spleen in fetus<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- All the above are correct<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-051\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">51- The membrane of RBCs allows the following except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increase the inner tension with the increase in volume<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pass within small capillaries without rupture<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Increase the surface area for gas exchange<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Keep hemoglobin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-052\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">52- The size of RBCs increases in venous blood because of:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Venous blood is more alkaline than arterial blood<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Carrying CO2<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Increased content of Na⁺ inside RBCs<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased content of K⁺ inside RBCs<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-053\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">53- The iron of the hemoglobin is eventually:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Converted into transferrin in the large intestine<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Converted into ferritin in the kidney<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Excreted from the body<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- All of the above<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- None of the above<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-054\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">54- All the following about hemoglobin is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It carries oxygen from the lungs to transport it to the tissues<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It contains 4 atoms of iron in the ferrous state<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It consists of 4 polypeptide chains and 4 heme groups<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- After it combines with oxygen molecules the iron changes to ferric state<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The globin part forms carbamino compounds with CO₂<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-055\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">55- hematocrit value of 45 % means that:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- 45% of the Hb is in the plasma.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- 45 % of the total blood volume is made up of plasma.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- 45 % of the total blood volume is made up of blood cells.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- 45 % of the Hb is in the red blood cells.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-056\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">56- The polypeptides in the globin part of normal adult Hb consists of:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- 2 alpha and 2 beta chains.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- 2 alpha and 2 gamma chains.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- 2 alpha and 2 delta chains.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- 2 beta and 2 gamma chains.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-057\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">57- Blood cell destruction occurs mainly in the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Bone marrow.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Kidneys<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Heart.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Spleen.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-058\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">58- About erythrocytes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- They contain no enzymes.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- They are responsible for the major part of blood viscosity.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Their life span is about 2 months.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Their Hb content carries only O2.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-059\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">59- Erythropoiesis in adult individuals occurs normally in the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Liver.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Red bone marrow.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Yellow bone marrow.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Spleen.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-060\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">60- In the following, mark the wrong statement:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Some substances (e.g. thyroid hormones) circulate bound to plasma proteins to increase their buffering capacity.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hb is present inside the R.B.Cs to prevent its escape to the plasma and excretion in the urine.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Erythropoiesis is increased in normal animals when injected with plasma obtained from hypoxic animals.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-061\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">61- About the active erythropoietic tissue, all the following is true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is not found in the vertebrae of adults.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is present early in intrauterine life.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It occupies the whole bone marrow at birth.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It is replaced by fat in the shafts of long bones in healthy adults.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-062\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">62- Erythropoiesis:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Occurs in the liver during the first 5 years of life<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Above 20 occurs in the bone marrow of all bones<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is affected by vitamin K deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is stimulated at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is more stimulated in females than males<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-063\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">63- Concerning erythropoiesis all is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is decreased after bone marrow depression<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Needs healthy liver for formation of globin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Needs healthy kidney for formation of 15% of erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is stimulated by testosterone hormone<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Increases in response to hypoxia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-064\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">64- Concerning erythropoiesis all is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is decreased after bone marrow depression<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Needs healthy liver for formation of globin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Needs healthy kidney for formation of 15% of erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is stimulated by testosterone hormone<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-065\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">65- Erythropoietin is essential for:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Leukopoiesis.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Formation of prothrombin.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Formation of red blood corpuscles.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- None of the above.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-066\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">66- Erythropoietin hormone:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is secreted mainly by the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is secreted mainly by the pancreas<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Stimulates RBCs formation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Stimulates WBCs formation<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-067\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">67- The main site of production of erythropoietin is the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Liver.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bone marrow.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Spleen.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Kidneys.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-068\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">68- Erythropoietin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is secreted by red bone marrow<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is stimulated by estrogen hormone<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is a component of hemoglobin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is secreted 85% from the liver and 15% from the bone marrow<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is elevated in persons living at high altitude<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-069\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">69- Erythropoietin hormone:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is secreted by the kidney 85% and the bone marrow 15%<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is stimulated by cobalt salts and acidosis at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Stimulates mitosis of the sensitive uncommitted stem cells<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Speeds all steps of development of proerythroblasts to mature RBCs<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-070\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">70- Erythropoietin hormone is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Secreted by the kidney 15% and the liver 85%<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Stimulated by acidosis at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Synthesized and released by red blood cell<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Inhibited by adenosine antagonists<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-071\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">71- A 36-year-old man with end stage renal disease has normocytic normochromic anemia. Which of the following is the most appropriate therapy?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Ferrous sulphate<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Folic acid<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitamin B6<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Vitamin B₁₂<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-072\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">72- Erythrocytes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Synthesize and release erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Have a higher concentration of potassium than is in plasma<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Have an abundant supply of mitochondria<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Have a multilobed nucleus<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Have about a 7 day survival time after release into the blood<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- Contain major histocompatibility protein (MHC) class I<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-073\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">73- The synthesis and release of erythropoietin is increased in a person who goes to live at high altitude because:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Cardiac output is increased<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hematocrit is increased<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Partial pressure of oxygen is less<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Alveolar ventilation rate is increased<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-074\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">74- Concerning erythropoiesis all the following statements are correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It occurs in the liver and spleen during fetal life.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- All blood cells are derived from a common uncommitted stem cell.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Erythropoietin hormone is secreted mainly by the liver.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It is inhibited after exposure to atomic radiation.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-075\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">75- Concerning the RBC:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It has a diameter of about 5 µm<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Contain hemoglobin, ribosomes and mitochondria<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is produced by the liver and spleen in fetus<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increase the inner tension with the increase in volume<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-076\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">76- Concerning erythropoiesis:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Needs healthy liver for formation of Heme<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Needs healthy kidney for formation of 15% of erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is stimulated by testosterone and thyroxine hormones<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Occurs in the liver during the first 5 years of life<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-077\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">77- The synthesis and release of erythropoietin is increased in a person who goes to live at high altitude because:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Partial pressure of oxygen is less<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Cardiac output is increased<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Acidosis at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Alveolar ventilation rate is increased<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-078\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">78- A 36-year-old man with end stage renal disease has normocytic normochromic anemia. Which of the following is the most appropriate therapy?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ferrous sulphate<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Folic acid<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitamin B12<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t05\"><h3>Vitamin B12 <small>— 17 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t05\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-079\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">79- Concerning Vitamin B12 absorption:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It needs intrinsic factor secreted by parietal cells of duodenum<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is absorbed by simple diffusion at lower ileum<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is transported in blood bound to transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Deficiency of pancreatic trypsin decreases its rate of absorption<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-080\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">80- Concerning Vitamin B12 absorption:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It needs intrinsic factor secreted by parietal cells of duodenum<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Absorbed by pinocytosis at lower ileum<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is transported in blood bound to transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Deficiency of pancreatic trypsin increases its rate of absorption<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-081\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">81- Improper maturation of the red blood corpuscles can be caused by:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Vitamin B12 deficiency.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hypoxia.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Iron deficiency.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Bone marrow aplasia.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-082\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">82- The intrinsic factor:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is found in the liver.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is produced by the gastric parietal cells.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is secreted by the terminal ileum.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Aids absorption of folic acid.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-083\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">83- Vitamin B₁₂ or folic acid deficiency produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Erythroblastic cells of the bone marrow to become smaller than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The adult red blood cells to become smaller than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The adult red blood cells to have a thicker membrane than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The adult red blood cells to become larger than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The adult red blood cells to exhibit increased osmotic fragility<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-084\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">84- Vitamin B₁₂:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Deficiency produces normocytic anemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Needs gastric HCl for its absorption<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is absorbed from the upper part of the small intestine<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is needed for nuclear maturation and cell division.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is stored in the bone marrow<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-085\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">85- Synthesis of DNA and cell division requires:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Iron<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Vitamin B₁₂ and folic acid<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Proteins of plant origin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitamin C<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-086\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">86- Macrocytic anemia is due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Chronic blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bone marrow depression<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Iron deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitamin B12 or folic acid deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Acute blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- RBCs hemolysis<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-087\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">87- Vitamin B12 deficiency may<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Result from disease of the proximal part of the ileum.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Result in anemia with small RBCs well filled with haemoglobin.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Cause a reduction in the circulating platelet level.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cause pathological changes in the central nervous system.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-088\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">88- Failure to absorb vitamin B₁₂ from the gastrointestinal tract results in a disease called:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Hypochromic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pernicious anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Polycythemia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Thalassaemia<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Normochromic anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-089\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">89- All the following substances are essential for the normal development of R.B.Cs except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Folic acid.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Ascorbic acid.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Nicotinic acid.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cyanocobalamine.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-090\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">90- Why is vitamin B12 necessary for erythropoiesis?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It's necessary for the ejection of the RBC nucleus<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It's necessary for DNA synthesis<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It's essential for protein aggregation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It's essential for oxygen's nucleophilic reaction with hemoglobin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-091\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">91- Stomach plays important role in erythropoiesis because it:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Helps absorption of folic acid<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Helps absorption of B12 and iron<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Secretes erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Forms globin part of hemoglobin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-092\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">92- In pernicious anaemia:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The life span of R.B.C.s is longer than normal.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- There is microcytic hyperchromic anaemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The formation of macrocytes is decreased.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Decreased absorption of vitamin B12 is suspected.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-093\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">93- Pernicious anaemia may be all the following except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sometimes the result of the malabsorption syndrome.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Treated with iron.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The cause of peripheral neuropathy.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Associated with carcinoma of the stomach.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-094\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">94- Vitamin B12 deficiency may:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Result from disease of the duodenum<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Result in anemia with large fragile RBCs<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Decrease the formation of platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cause leucopenia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-095\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">95- Vitamin B12 or folic acid deficiency produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Erythroblastic cells of the bone marrow to become smaller than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The adult red blood cells to become smaller than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The adult red blood cells to have a thicker membrane than normal<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The adult red blood cells to become larger than normal<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t06\"><h3>Iron <small>— 26 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t06\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-096\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">96- As regard the iron required for hemoglobin synthesis:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ferric iron (Fe³⁺) is absorbed from the upper part of the small intestine<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is transported in the blood in the form of transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Its deficiency produces macrocytic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The greatest percentage of ferritin is found in the bone marrow<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-097\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">97- Iron:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is absorbed as ferrous (Fe²⁺) iron by a passive process<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is decreased in acute blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is stored in the liver in the form of transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Needs vitamin C for absorption<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Deficiency produces pernicious anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-098\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">98- Iron absorption:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Occurs when the iron is in the ferric state (Fe³⁺)<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Requires gastric HCl<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is a passive process which depends on the body requirements<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Occurs in the lower part of the small intestine<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-099\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">99- Microcytic hypochromic anemia is due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Decrease vitamin B₁₂ intake<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decrease iron intake<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Diseases of the heart<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Diseases of the lung<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Acute massive bleeding<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-100\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">100- All about iron absorption is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Antacids reduce iron absorption<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heme iron is better absorbed than non-heme iron<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Ferrous iron (Fe²⁺) is better absorbed than ferric iron (Fe³⁺)<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The majority of iron absorption occurs in terminal ileum<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-101\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">101- Which of the following statements about iron metabolism is correct?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ferritin is a plasma protein that transports iron in the blood<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hemosiderin is a product of hemoglobin degradation<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Iron is more efficiently absorbed in the ferrous state than in the ferric state<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Most iron in the body is stored as hemosiderin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The gastrointestinal rate of iron absorption is extremely high<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-102\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">102- Iron deficiency:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is more common in males than in females<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- May cause anemia by inhibiting the rate of multiplication of RBCs stem cells<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Occurs due to chronic blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- May cause large pale erythrocytes to appear in peripheral blood<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Anemia must be treated by iron injection<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-103\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">103- In the blood, iron is primarily transported by:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Hemosiderin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Ferritin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Stercobilin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Transferrin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-104\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">104- The major protein that transports iron in the plasma from the site of absorption to cells engaged in erythropoiesis is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Hepcidin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Ferritin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Hemosiderin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-105\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">105- Most of the iron in the body is present in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Hemoglobin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Myoglobin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Ferritin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Transferrin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-106\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">106- About iron deficiency anaemia:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is more common in men than in women.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is characterized by large pale erythrocytes.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is typically found following chronic blood loss from the body.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It occurs in gastric diseases associated with lack of the intrinsic factor.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-107\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">107- The production of erythrocytes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is decreased in high altitudes.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Occurs in the spleen in normal adults.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is stimulated by an increase in the arterial PCO2.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is decreased if the stomach loses the ability to produce a normal gastric juice.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-108\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">108- The red cells in iron deficiency anemia are:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Normocytic normochromic.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Spherocytic cells.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Microcytic hypochromic<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Macrocytic hyperchromic.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-109\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">109- An 18-year-old girl was prescribed iron supplement by her doctor as she was thought to take a diet deficient in iron. Lack of iron often causes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Polycythemia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hypochromic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Pernicious anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Megaloblastic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Normochromic anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-110\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">110- Hepcidin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Stimulates formation of ferroportin molecules in macrophages<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Secretion is inhibited by inflammation and hypoxia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Inhibits the release of recycled iron from macrophage<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is a hormone secreted by the enterocyte to regulate iron intestinal absorption<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-111\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">111- Which of the following protein is a regulator for iron absorption by enterocytes<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ferritin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hemosiderin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Hepcidin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Transferrin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-112\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">112- Which of the following statements about iron metabolism is correct?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ferritin is a plasma protein that transports iron in the blood<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Iron is more efficiently absorbed in the ferrous state than in the ferric state<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Most iron in the body is stored as hemosiderin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The gastrointestinal rate of iron absorption is extremely high<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-113\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">113- Iron deficiency:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is more common in males than in females<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- May cause anemia by inhibiting the division of RBCs stem cells<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- May cause small pale erythrocytes to appear in peripheral blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Occurs due to acute blood loss<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-114\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">114- Iron deficiency:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is more common in males than in females<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- May cause anemia by inhibiting the division of RBCs stem cells<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Occurs due to chronic blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- May cause large pale erythrocytes to appear in peripheral blood<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-115\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">115- Stomach plays important role in erythropoiesis because It:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Helps absorption of folic acid<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Helps absorption of B12 and iron<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Secretes erythropoietin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Forms globin part of hemoglobin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-116\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">116- Iron absorption is characterized by all of the following EXCEPT:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It needs vitamin C to facilitate its absorption<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heme iron is directly absorbed through heme carrier protein<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It occurs at the distal part of the small intestine<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Absorbed iron is carried by transferrin in plasma<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-117\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">117- Iron:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is decreased in acute blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is stored in the liver in the form of transferrin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Needs vitamin C for absorption<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Deficiency produces pernicious anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-118\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">118- Iron absorption:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Occurs when the iron is in the ferric state (Fe3*)<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Requires gastric HCl<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is a passive process which depends on the body requirements<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Occurs in the lower part of the small intestine<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-119\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">119- Iron deficiency<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Frequently follows persistent loss of blood from the body.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is more common in men than in women.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Cause anemia by inhibiting the rate of multiplication of RBC stem cells.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- May cause large pale erythrocytes to appear in peripheral blood.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-120\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">120- About iron deficiency anaemia:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is more common in adult men<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is characterized by large pale erythrocytes.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is typically found following chronic blood loss from the body.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It occurs in gastric diseases associated with lack of intrinsic factor.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-121\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">121- An 18-year-old girl was prescribed iron supplement by her doctor as she was thought to take a diet deficient in iron. Lack of iron often causes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Polycythemia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hypochromic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Pernicious anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Normochromic anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t07\"><h3>Anemia &amp; Polycythemia <small>— 14 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t07\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-122\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">122- All the following conditions cause anemia except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Erythroblastosis fetalis.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Vitamin B12 deficiency.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Hypothyroidism.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Living at high altitudes.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-123\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">123- Severe depression of the bone marrow may result in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Microcytic hypochromic anaemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Increased number of granulocytes.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Aplastic anaemia, leucopenia, and thrombocytopenia.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased coagulability of the blood.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-124\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">124- The red blood corpuscles:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Haemolyze when placed in a hypertonic solution.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Are smaller than normal in case of folic acid deficiency.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Are normal in size in anemia due to bone marrow depression.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-125\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">125- Anemia results from all the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Living at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bone marrow depression<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Atrophy of gastric mucosa<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Iron deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Folic acid deficiency<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-126\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">126- Excessive destruction of erythrocytes is characteristic of:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Aplastic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pernicious anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Hemolytic anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-127\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">127- Concerning polycythemia the following is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Occurs in liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Increases the viscosity of the blood<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Can occur in someone who lives at high altitude<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Can result from a high level of erythropoietin secretion<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-128\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">128- Increased R. B.Cs fragility occurs in all the following cases except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sickle cell anaemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Iron deficiency anaemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Hereditary spherocytosis<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-129\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">129- Polycythemia may occur in all the following conditions except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Tumor of the kidney.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Right to left shunts in the heart.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Advanced liver disease.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- High altitudes.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-130\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">130- Severe depression of the bone marrow may result in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Microcytic hypochromic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Increased number of granulocytes<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Aplastic anemia, leucopenia, and thrombocytopenia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased coagulability of the blood<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-131\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">131- Causes of Microcytic Hypochromic anemia, all are true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Iron deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Acute bleeding<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Partial gastrectomy<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Excessive menses<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-132\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">132- Conditions cause normocytic normochromic anemia, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Acute hemorrhage<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hemolytic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Aplastic anemia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Folic acid deficiency anemia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-133\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">133- Microcytic hypochromic anemia is due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Decrease vitamin B12 intake<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decrease iron intake<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Diseases of the heart<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Diseases of the lung<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-134\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">134- Macrocytic anemia is due to<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Chronic blood loss<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bone marrow depression<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Iron deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitamin B12 or folic acid deficiency<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-135\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">135- Normocytic Normochromic anemia is characterized by:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Normal RBCs count, normal RBCs size and normal hemoglobin content<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Normal RBCs count, normal RBCs size and low hemoglobin content<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Normal RBCs count, normal RBCs size and normal PCV<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Normal RBCs size, low RBCs count and low hemoglobin content<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t08\"><h3>Hemostasis <small>— 37 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t08\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-136\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">136- The first phase of hemostasis is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Separation of globin and heme<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Activation of Prothrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Platelet aggregation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vascular spasm<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-137\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">137- Thromboxane A₂:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Causes platelet aggregation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is metabolized to prostacyclin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is directly inactivated by binding to aspirin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Converts prothrombin to thrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is released by erythrocytes<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-138\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">138- The phase of coagulation that begins with exposed endothelial collagen is the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Extrinsic pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Intrinsic pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Common pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Fibrin stabilization phase<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-139\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">139- Contact of the blood with sub- endothelial collagen produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Inhibition of platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Activation of factor VII<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Activation of factor XII<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Activation of factor IX<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-140\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">140- Blood coagulation:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Through the extrinsic pathway is initiated by contact of blood with a negatively charged surface<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Through the intrinsic pathway does not occur outside the body<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Through the intrinsic pathway is initiated by tissue damage<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Through the extrinsic pathway is initiated by the release of tissue thromboplastin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Results from conversion of thrombin to prothrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- Can occur in the absence of calcium<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-141\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">141- The correct sequence of activation of extrinsic pathway of blood coagulation is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Tissue thromboplastin activates factor VIII<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Calcium ions activate factor VII<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Tissue thromboplastin activates factor VII<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Tissue thromboplastin activates factor IX<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Collagen fibers activate factor XII<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-142\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">142- Which sequence is correct for the following events? 1. Fibrinogen --&gt; Fibrin 2. Clot retraction 3. Formation of thromboplastin 4. Prothrombin --&gt; Thrombin<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- 1,2,3,4<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- 3,4,1,2<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- 4,3,1,2<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- 3,2,1,4<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-143\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">143- The following are vitamin K dependent clotting factors, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Prothrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Factor XII<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Factor VII<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Factor X<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-144\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">144- Vitamin K dependent clotting factors include:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Factor IX<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Factor XI<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fibrinogen<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Plasminogen<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-145\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">145- The final reaction in the formation of a blood clot:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The formation of prothrombin activator<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Thrombin converts fibrinogen to fibrin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Prothrombin activator converts prothrombin to thrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Hageman factor activates prothrombin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-146\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">146- When a blood vessel wall is injured, platelets induce the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Vascular spasm and temporary plug formation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Exposure of platelet phospholipid (PL)<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Initiation of extrinsic pathway of coagulation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Stabilization of fibrin and clot retraction<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-147\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">147- Tissue thromboplastin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is also known as factor V<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is the cell surface receptor for factor VIa<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Complexes with factor VIIa to catalyze the activation of factor X<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is an important component of the intrinsic coagulation pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is normally expressed by endothelial cells<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-148\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">148- Factor VII:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is a cofactor in the coagulation cascade<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Initiates the process of coagulation with tissue thromboplastin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is vitamin-K- independent<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is produced by platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Deficiency is common<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-149\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">149- Which of the following statements regarding coagulation is correct?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Extrinsic pathway activation follows contact of blood with collagen<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It results from conversion of thrombin to prothrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Prekallikrein is converted to kallikrein during activation of extrinsic pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Thrombin converts fibrinogen to fibrin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Vitamin K is an essential co-factor for hepatic synthesis of factor VIII<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-150\" data-k=\"f\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">150- Normal blood clotting requires:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Inactivation of heparin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Inactivation of plasmin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Adequate intake of vitamin C<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Adequate intake of vitamin K<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Calcium ions<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- Both (d) and (e) are correct<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-151\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">151- The conversion of fibrinogen to fibrin:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is affected by prothrombin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is stimulated by heparin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is reversed by plasmin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is followed by polymerization of fibrin monomers<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-152\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">152- Which of the following is not involved in coagulation?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Gamma globulins<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Calcium<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Vitamin K<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Prothrombin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-153\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">153- Anti thrombin III activity is increased by:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Aspirin<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Citrate<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Coumarin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Heparin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Warfarin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-154\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">154- Protein C:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is a major physiological anticoagulant<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decreases the formation of plasmin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is activated by prothrombin to activated protein C<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- In its activated form degrades factor VII<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is a breakdown product of C-reactive protein<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-155\" data-k=\"d\" data-alt=\"\" data-fx=\"الـthrombomodulin بيرتبط بالـthrombin ويكوّن مركّبًا بينشّط الـprotein C (مش protein S)، والـprotein S عامل مساعد للـprotein C المنشَّط. فنص الاختيار D غالبًا خطأ مطبعي (المقصود protein C).\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">155- Thrombomodulin:<span class=\"gtag warn\" dir=\"rtl\">مفتاح الملزمة مشكوك فيه<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is secreted by RBCs<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is activated by heparin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Activates platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Binds with thrombin forming a complex that activates protein S<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-156\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">156- Which of the following is a feature of protein S:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is synthesized by the endothelium<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Its synthesis requires vitamin C<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It functions as a cofactor to protein C<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It is involved in the inactivation of factor IXa<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is involved in the inactivation of factor Xa<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-157\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">157- About the action of anticoagulants, all of the following is true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Dicumarol interferes with the synthesis of prothrombin in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Oxalates form insoluble salts with Ca²⁺<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Citrates and other chelating agents bind Ca²⁺<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Heparin blocks the action of antithrombin III<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-158\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">158- Concerning plasmin one of the following is not correct:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is a proteolytic enzyme<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is formed from plasminogen<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Digests fibrin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Digests fibrinogen<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Has a direct Antithrombin activity<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-159\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">159- Which of the following activates platelets during hemostasis?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Eosinophil degranulation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Exposed collagen or endothelial basement membrane<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Fibrin thread formation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Thromboplastin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-160\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">160- Which one of the following anticoagulants is preferred for storage of donated blood?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Citrate<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Coumarin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Heparin<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Oxalate<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-161\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">161- Bleeding time is prolonged in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Deficiency of factor VIII<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Malabsorption of vitamin K<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Intake of coumarin derivatives<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Intake of large quantities of aspirin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-162\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">162- Prolonged bleeding time may be due to all of the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Thrombocytopenia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Hemophilia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Excessive oral intake of aspirin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Both b and c<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-163\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">163- Regarding bleeding from a small cut in the skin all is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is diminished by local vascular spasm<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Stops within about 5 minutes in normal people<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is prolonged in severe factor VIII deficiency<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is greater from warm skin than from cold skin<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is reduced if the affected limb is elevated<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-164\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">164- Deficiency of factor VIII:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increases the bleeding time<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is due to an abnormal gene on the Y chromosome<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Affects the extrinsic, rather than the intrinsic, pathway for blood coagulation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increases the clotting time<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Causes small (petechial) hemorrhages into the skin to cause purpura<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-165\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">165- Obstruction of common bile duct by a stone will increase bleeding tendency due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Decreased formation of factor XII in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decreased platelet count<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Decreased synthesis of vitamin k in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Decreased synthesis of prothrombin<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-166\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">166- How does aspirin influence platelet’s function:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Impairs process of their aggregation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decreases their content<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Reduces bleeding time<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Reduces their life span<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Has no influence<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-167\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">167- Which of the following statements about blood coagulation is correct?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Absence of Ca²⁺ promotes blood coagulation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Patients with hemophilia A usually have a normal bleeding time<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Von Willebrand factor suppresses platelet adhesion<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Von Willebrand factor suppresses blood coagulation<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-168\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">168- Which of the following conditions is associated with a depression of the coagulation process and excessive bleeding after surgery?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Gastrointestinal disease<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heart disease<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Kidney disease<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Pulmonary disease<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-169\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">169- Factor XI:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is produced by platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is a member of the extrinsic pathway<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Activates factor X<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Deficiency causes hemophilia C<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Is formed by the spleen<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-170\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">170- Factor IX:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is a co-factor in the coagulation cascade<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is activated by factor V<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Requires prostacyclin for its activity<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Acts by converting factor X to Xa<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Deficiency causes hemophilia A<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-171\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">171- A patient with prolonged activated partial thromboplastin time (APTT). The most likely cause is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Heparin therapy<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Liver disease<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Malabsorption of vitamin K<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Poor factor VII synthesis<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Warfarin therapy<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-172\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">172- About intravascular clotting, all the following is true, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It occurs by intrinsic system of coagulation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is induced by slowing of blood flow<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is related to clumping of platelets<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It does not occur normally because Ca²⁺ is present<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- It occurs with accumulation of lipids in the arterial wall<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph1_t09\"><h3>Blood Groups &amp; Rh <small>— 13 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph1_t09\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-173\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">173- Which of the following people would have the most anti-B antibodies?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- An adult male with B+ blood<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- An adult male with O- blood<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- An adult female with B− blood<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- A female child with AB+ blood<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-174\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">174- A person has type O+ blood, then which of the following is true?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- He has no agglutinins at all<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- He has no A agglutinogens<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- He has no Rh agglutinogens<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- None of the above<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-175\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">175- A person’s blood type was determined to be AB+. Which of the following is true?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- There are no antibodies to antigens A, B, or Rh in the plasma<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The RBCs contain the A and B antigens on their nuclei<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The blood totally lacks the Rh factor<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- He cannot receive blood from someone who is type O negative<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-176\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">176- Which of the following females does not have to be concerned with erythroblastosis fetalis?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- A female with blood type O-<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- A female with blood type O+<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- A female with blood type AB-<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- A female with blood type B+<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- B and d<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-177\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">177- An individual with type B+ blood has which of the following antibodies in their blood?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Anti-A and anti-O<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Anti-B and anti-Rh<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Anti-A<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Anti-B<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Anti-Rh<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-178\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">178- An individual who is blood type AB negative:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Can receive any blood type in moderate amounts except that with the Rh antigen<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Can donate to all blood types in moderate amounts<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Can receive types A, B, and AB but not type O<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Can donate to types A, B, and AB but not to type O<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-179\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">179- Blood type O persons are considered universal donors due to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Type O blood has the commonest distribution<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Their RBCs contain neither A nor B agglutinogens<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Their RBCs may contain the Rh-factor<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Their plasma contains both alpha and beta agglutinins<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- They receive blood from all groups<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-180\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">180- A group B Rh-ve person can receive blood for the 2nd time from:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Group AB Rh –ve<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Group O Rh –ve<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Group O Rh +ve<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Group B Rh +ve<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Group A Rh -ve<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-181\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">181- Before blood transfusion, which of the following should be done?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- ESR<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Osmotic fragility test<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Blood indices<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cross matching test<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-182\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">182- Immunoglobulin G:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is produced in large amounts during the primary immune response<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Includes ABO group antibodies<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Activates interferons<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Can cross the placenta to reach the fetus<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Has the largest molecular weight<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-183\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">183- Which one of the following represents the most dangerous situation?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- An Rh-positive mother who is bearing her second Rh-negative child<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- An Rh-negative mother who is bearing her second Rh-positive child<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- An Rh-positive mother who is bearing her first Rh-negative child<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- An Rh-negative mother who is bearing her first Rh-positive child<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The transfusion of O-negative blood into an A-positive recipient<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-184\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">184- All the following statements regarding the ABO and rhesus (Rh) systems are true, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- A person of group O is a universal donor<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- A person who is group AB has anti-A and anti-B antibodies<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The presence of the D antigen means that the subject is Rh+ve<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The second Rh+ve baby of a Rh-ve mother is at a greater risk than the first<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph1m-185\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">185- Erythroblastosis fetalis:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Affects mainly babies of Rh-positive mothers<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Occurs mainly in babies who lack D agglutinogens<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Occurs mainly during the 1st pregnancy<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Can be prevented by injecting the mother with anti-D antibodies just after delivery<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><\/div><div class=\"gpart\" data-part=\"2\" data-ch=\"p2\"><h2 dir=\"ltr\">Chapter 2 · Autonomic Nervous System <small>— الجهاز العصبي اللاإرادي · 100 سؤال · <bdi dir=\"ltr\">Dr. Mohamed Maher MCQs<\/bdi><\/small><\/h2><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph2_t01\"><h3>Introduction &amp; Autonomic Ganglia <small>— 16 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph2_t01\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-001\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">1- The system that controls smooth muscle, cardiac muscle, and gland activity is the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Somatic nervous system<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Autonomic nervous system<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Skeletal division<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Sensory nervous system<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-002\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">2- One of the following is not supplied by autonomic nervous system:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Heart<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Lungs<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Stomach<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Skeletal muscles<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Iris<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-003\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">3- The peripheral nervous system includes the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Somatic nervous system.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Brain.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Spinal cord.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Nuclei.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-004\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">4- Which of the following structures is a component of reflex arc?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Afferent neuron .<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Efferent neuron .<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Sensory receptor.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Effector organ.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- All of the above.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-005\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">5- The somatic nervous system is part of the<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sympathetic nervous system.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Parasympathetic nervous system.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Autonomic nervous system.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- None of the above.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-006\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">6- The following reflexes are all autonomic Except<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Salivary secretion.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Micturition.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Flexion of the arm following a painful stimulus.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Acceleration of the heart.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-007\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">7- What is the autonomic nervous system?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Part of the central nervous system independent of the will.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The efferent pathway to the viscera (all fibers connecting the CNS to glands, smooth muscles and heart).<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- All efferent fibers in the body except those to smooth muscle.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Afferent (sensory) fibers from the bone.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-008\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">8- The autonomic nervous system differs from the somatic nervous system in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Has a preganglionc neuron which comes outside the CNS and a postganglionic neuron which supplies the organ<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Originates from all segments of the spinal cord<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Has no control on the heart<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Originates from the anterior horn cells<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Releases one type of chemical transmitters only<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-009\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">9- A modular body which contains large numbers of neuronal cell bodies and is located within the peripheral neurons system is called<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Ganglion.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Nerve.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Nucleus.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Tract.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Plexus.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-010\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">10- Autonomic ganglia are:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Present inside CNS<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Distribution centers<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- 3 types<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Site of relay between 8-9 preganglionic and one postganglionic neurons<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Contain the cell bodies of preganglionic neurons<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-011\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">11- The autonomic ganglia:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are 5 types.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Are the sites of relay of afferent neurons.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Function as distributing centres.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Are located inside the CNS.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Are relay stations for all pregang . fibers passing through them .<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-012\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">12- The sympathetic preganglionic nerve fibres:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Arise from the cervical segments of the spinal cord.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Originate at the autonomic ganglia.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Are myelinated nerve fibers belonging to the B group of the nerve Fibers.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Show minimal divergence (branching) in the autonomic ganglia.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Those supply the abdominal viscera relay in the sympathetic chain<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-013\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">13- Regarding autonomic ganglia:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Paravertebral chain has 5 ganglia at cervical region<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Collateral ganglia are only parasympathetic ganglia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Adrenal medulla is supplied by preganglionic adrenergic fibers<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Terminal ganglia can be present in the viscera<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Terminal ganglia are modified sympathetic ganglia<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-014\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">14- The following is true about the autonomic nervous system, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The postganglionic neurons are largely unmyelinated<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- All preganglionic neurons are cholinergic<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The preganglionic neurons of the sympathetic nervous system are shorter than the parasympathetic nervous system<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The parasympathetic outflow is only found in the cranial nerves<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The sympathetic preganglionic neurons arise from the lateral horn cells of segments T1-L3<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-015\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">15- The two major division of the autonomic system are the sympathetic and parasympathetic. Where do parasympathetic fibers originate?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The thoraco-lumbar spinal region.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The cranial and sacral regions.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-016\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">16- Effector organs of the ANS include all of the following EXCEPT:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Medulla<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Arteriolar smooth muscle.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Heart.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Visceral smooth muscles.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Glands.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph2_t02\"><h3>Sympathetic <small>— 9 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph2_t02\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-017\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">17- Damage to the left cervical sympathetic chain ganglia ( Horner's syndrome) produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increased sweat secretion on the left side of the face<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pale skin on the left side of the face<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Ptosis on the left side<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Pupil dilation of the left eye<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Inhibition of salivary gland secretion<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-018\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">18- Dropping of the eyelid ( ptosis ) is caused by damage to :<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The third cranial nerve.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The parasympathetic supply to the eye.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The sympathetic supply to the eye.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Lesion in lumbar 2,3.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-019\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">19- Sympathetic stimulation of the iris causes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Astigmatism.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pupillary constriction.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Pupillary dilation.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Vitreous secretion.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-020\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">20- Generalized sympathetic activity is characterized by the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Contraction of the radial muscle in the iris<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Increased urinary excretion of catecholamines<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Lipolysis in adipose tissue<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Decreased conduction rate in the atrioventricular bundle<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Contraction of sphincteric smooth muscles of gastrointestinal tract<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-021\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">21- The sympathetic response in a \"fight or flight\" reaction causes a decrease in the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Arterial blood pressure<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Diameter of the pupil<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Resistance of the airways<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Blood glucose concentration<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Heart rate<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-022\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">22- Stimulation of the greater splanchnic nerve produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increased motility of the plain muscles of stomach<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Excessive secretion of gastric juice<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Decreased blood glucose level<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Secretion of epinephrine and norepinephrine by the adrenal medulla<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Inhibition of mictuirition<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-023\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">23- Stimulation of the greater splanchnic nerve produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increased motility of the stomach &amp; upper half of the small intestine.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Inhibition of micturition.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Increased blood levels of both glucose &amp; catecholamines.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- V.C. of the blood vessels in the erectile tissue of both males &amp; females.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Increased secretion by both the stomach &amp; pancreas.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-024\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">24- Preganglionic sympathetic nerve fibers:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are found in somatic nerves (e.g., median &amp; ulnar nerves).<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Are present in the short ciliary nerves.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Are non – myelinated.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Are found in the greater splanchnic nerves.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-025\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">25- The sympathetic supply is not responsible for:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Constriction of the pupil.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Erection of hair.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Secretion of eccrine sweat glands.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Dilatation of skeletal muscle blood vessels.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Spleen contraction.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph2_t03\"><h3>Parasympathetic <small>— 24 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph2_t03\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-026\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">26- The efferent nerves that stimulate salivary secretion include:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Chorda tympani<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- sympathetic nerves<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Vagus nerve<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Glossopharyngeal nerve<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Both a and d<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-027\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">27- Salivary secretion caused by parasympathetic stimulation is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Watery<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Small in volume<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Rich in mucus<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Poor in amylase<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-028\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">28- The action of parasympathetic in the salivary glands is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Vasoconstriction and secretion<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Vasodilation and secretion<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Vasodilation and inhibition of secretion<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Secretion of small amount of viscous saliva<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-029\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">29- One of the following is not supplied by parasympathetic fibers:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Atria<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Ventricles<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Gall bladder<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Salivary glands<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-030\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">30- Blockade of parasympathetic activity causes a reduction in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sweat production<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Heart rate<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Strength of skeletal muscle contraction<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Salivation<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Lipolysis<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-031\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">31- The efferent impulses that stimulate salivary secretion proceed along all the following nerves except the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Chorda tympani.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Sympathetic nerves.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Occulomotor nerve.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Glossopharyngeal nerve.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-032\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">32- Parasympathetic nerves:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Have opposite effects to sympathetic nerves on intestinal smooth muscle<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Have opposite effects to sympathetic nerves on iris smooth muscle<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Cause vasodilatation in skeletal muscle during prolonged exercise<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cause sweat secretion in skin when body temperature rises<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Have longer postganglionic than preganglionic fibers<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-033\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">33- Most of the parasympathetic outflow is provided by:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The pelvic nerves<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The vagus nerve<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The collateral ganglia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The glossopharyngeal nerve<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-034\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">34- About the vagus nerve, all the following is true except<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It originates mainly from medulla oblongata.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It contains parasympathetic preganglionic Fibers.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It has no direct effect on ventricular contraction.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It causes increased peristaltic movements of the intestinal wall.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- It produces micturition.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-035\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">35- Stimulation of the vagus nerves produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- A reduction in the force of ventricular contraction<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Secretion and vasodilatation in the salivary glands<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Bronchodilation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Contraction of the spleen<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Contraction of gallbladder<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-036\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">36- Stimulation of vagus nerve does not produce:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increased heart rate and Pulmonary vasoconstriction<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Increased gastric secretion<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Contraction of the wall of the gall bladder<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Prolongation of cardiac conduction<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-037\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">37- About the vagus nerve, all the following is true except<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It originates mainly from medulla oblongata.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It contains parasympathetic preganglionic Fibers.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It has no direct effect on ventricular contraction.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It causes increased peristaltic movements of the intestinal wall.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- It produces micturition.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-038\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">38- Parasympathetic neurons are inhibitory to smooth muscles in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The ciliary muscle<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Dilator pupillae muscle<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The bronchial tree<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Mucosal blood vessels<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-039\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">39- Stimulation of the pelvic nerves produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Relaxation of the wall of rectum and contraction of internal anal sphincter<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Vasoconstriction of blood vessels causing erection of penis<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Contraction of the bladder wall and relaxation of internal urethral sphincter<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Ejaculation of semen<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Relaxation of the external urethral and anal sphincters<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-040\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">40- An injury to the first 4 sacral segments of the spinal cord produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Hyperglycemia.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- V.D. in the Cutaneous blood vessels.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Disturbance of sweat secretion.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Lack of erection of the penis in males<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Relaxation of the internal anal &amp; urethral sphincters.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-041\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">41- Stimulation of the sacral autonomic (pelvic nerve) supply produces:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Inhibition of the plain muscles of the wall of the urinary bladder<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Erection<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Contraction of the wall of rectum and the internal anal sphincter<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Gastric HCl and pepsin secretion<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-042\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">42- Stimulation of the pelvic nerve causes:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Contraction of the bronchial muscle.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Contraction of the internal urethral &amp; rectal (anal) sphincters.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- V.D. of the blood vessels in the external genitalia.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Stoppage of prostatic secretions.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Urine retention<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-043\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">43- Regarding the pelvic nerve, the following is true Except<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is the nerve of erection (= nerves erigents).<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is motor to the urinary bladder &amp; distal half of the large intestine.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is inhibitory to both the internal anal &amp; urethral sphincters.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It has both preganglionic &amp; postganglionic nerve fibres.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Its functions are normally under continuous inhibition.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-044\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">44- Parasympathetic stimulation produces all of the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Decreased heart rate<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bronchodilation<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Increased gastric secretion<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Urination<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Defecation<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-045\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">45- Which of the following is not caused by parasympathetic stimulation?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Micturition<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Miosis<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Increased GIT motility<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Sweating<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-046\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">46- Which of the following visceral tissues receives sympathetic postganglionic neurons only?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Adrenal medulla<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Sweat glands<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Anal sphincters<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The iris<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-047\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">47- Which of the following may be produced by parasympathetic Stimulation:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Acceleration of the heart.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Contraction of the urinary bladder wall.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- V.D. of skeletal muscle blood vessels.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Dilatation of the pupil.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Relaxation of the GIT wall.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-048\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">48- The parasympathetic nervous system affects all of these organs EXCEPT:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Heart.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pupillary smooth muscles.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Salivary glands.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Adrenal glands.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-049\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">49- Which of the following structures is an example where double innervation does not apply?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The heart.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The bladder.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The stomach.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The intestines.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Splenic capsule.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><section class=\"tsec gsec\" data-g=\"ph2_t04\"><h3>Transmitters, Receptors &amp; Drugs <small>— 51 سؤال<\/small><\/h3><div class=\"tbar\"><button class=\"btn clear sm gclear\" type=\"button\" data-g=\"ph2_t04\">Clear<\/button><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-050\" data-k=\"f\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">50- Acetylcholine is a neurotransmitter at:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- sweat glands<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- the adrenal medulla<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- parasympathetic ganglia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- the parotid gland<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- the neuromuscular junction<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- all of the above<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-051\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">51- Acetylcholine is released from the following fibers, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- All parasympathetic preganglionic fibers<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- All parasympathetic postganglionic fibers<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- All sympathetic preganglionic fibers<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- All sympathetic postganglionic fibers<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-052\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">52- The sympathetic preganglionic neurons release….. at their terminals, and the effect is always ……..:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- norepinephrine ; inhibitory<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- norepinephrine ; excitatory<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- acetylcholine ; excitatory<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- acetylcholine ; inhibitory<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-053\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">53- Which of the following responses is mediated by parasympathetic muscarinic receptors?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Dilation of bronchial smooth muscles<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Erection<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Ejaculation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Constriction of GIT sphincters<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Increased cardiac contractility<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-054\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">54- Sympathetic and parasympathetic systems have cooperative effects on:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Cardiac activity<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Gastrointestinal activity<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Sexual activity<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The diameter of pupil<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-055\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">55- Parasympathetic innervation is antagonistic to sympathetic innervation on:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Constrictor pupillae muscle<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Cutaneous blood vessels<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Salivary glands secretion<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The act of micturition<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-056\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">56- The following about sympathetic nervous system is true except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- All its preganglionic fibers are cholinergic.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is involved in stress &amp; emergency conditions.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It has a V.D. effect on skeletal muscle blood vessels during rest.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Its stimulation increases the cardiac properties.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Its stimulation causes urine retention.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-057\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">57- The sympathetic nervous system has all of the following characters except<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is mostly noradrenergic.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is involved more frequently in generalized actions.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is of little importance in visual accommodation for near vision<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It antagonizes mostly parasympathetic functions.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- It is anabolic.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-058\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">58- Increased release of norepinephrine from the sympathetic nerves in the heart would:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increase heart rate<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decrease heart rate<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Directly dilate coronary vessels<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Decrease the force of cardiac contraction<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-059\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">59- Epinephrine is:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Synthesized in the adrenal medulla<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The chemical transmitter of most sympathetic postganglionic nerve fibers<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- More powerful as a pressor than norepinephrine<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Hydrolyzed by cholinesterase enzyme<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Released by the sympathetic cholinergic postganglionic nerve fibers<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-060\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">60- Nicotine in small doses stimulates the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Alpha adrenergic receptors.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Receptors at the organs supplied by parasympathetic postganglionic nerve fibers.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Receptors in the neurons present in the sympathetic chain<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Beta adrenergic receptors.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-061\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">61- It is true to say that nicotine in small dose has an excitatory influence on the<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Receptors located in the neurons present in the sympathetic chain (ganglia)<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Beta adrenergic receptors.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Alpha adrenergic receptors.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Receptors those are normally responsive to postganglionic Parasympathetic fibers.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-062\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">62- Nicotine like action of acetylcholine is present in:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- All preganglionic nerve endings<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The sympathetic postganglionic supply to the blood vessels in skeletal muscles<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The parasympathetic postganglionic supply to the heart<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The sympathetic postganglionic supply to the sweat glands<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The parasympathetic postganglionic supply to the GIT<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-063\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">63- Concerning the adrenal medulla, all of the following is true, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Acts in emergency situations<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Secretes epinephrine 80% and norepinephrine 20%<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Augments and prolongs the effect of sympathetic stimulation<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is a modified sympathetic ganglion<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Receives preganglionic fibers from the anterior horn cells of the lower 6 thoracic segments of the spinal cord<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-064\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">64- The effect of neurotransmitters on the effectors cells depends on:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- The nature of the receptor<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- The nature of the neurotransmitter<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- The number of the receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- None of the above<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-065\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">65- Nicotinic action of acetylcholine:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Is blocked by atropine<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Is excitatory to both intestinal movements and secretion<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is stimulatory to autonomic ganglia<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Is not affected by curare<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- has no effect on the neuromuscular transmission<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-066\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">66- Nicotinic receptors stimulation is responsible for:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increasing the excitability of sympathetic postganglionic neurons<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Increasing the force of stomach contractions<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Delaying the emptying of liquids from the stomach<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Decreasing the excitability of sympathetic postganglionic neurons<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-067\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">67- Which autonomic receptor is blocked at the ganglia, but not at the effector organs?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Adrenergic α receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Adrenergic β1 receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Adrenergic β2 receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cholinergic muscarinic receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Cholinergic nicotinic receptors<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-068\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">68- Which autonomic receptor mediates secretion of epinephrine by the adrenal medulla?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Adrenergic α receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Adrenergic β1 receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Adrenergic β2 receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cholinergic muscarinic receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Cholinergic nicotinic receptors<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-069\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">69- adrenal medulla:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Have both alpha and beta adrenergic receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Have cholinergic receptor<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Release more norepinephrine than epinephrine<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Are activated by adrenergic receptor agonist<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-070\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">70- Adenyl cyclase is activated by:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- β1 agonists<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- α2 agonists<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- α1 agonists<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- β2 agonist<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- a and d are correct<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-071\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">71- Which adrenergic receptor produces its stimulatory effects by increasing intracellular Ca2+ concentration?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- α1 receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- α2 receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- β1 receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- β2 receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Muscarinic receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"f\" tabindex=\"0\">f- Nicotinic receptors<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-072\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">72- Adrenergic receptors are classified into:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- α1- receptors which cause inhibition of adenyl cyclase<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- β1- receptors which increase the cardiac properties through increased cAMP in the cell<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- α2- receptors which increase intracellular calcium ions<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- β2- receptors which cause contraction of the bronchial muscles<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-073\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">73- The α- adrenergic receptors produces all the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Vasoconstriction<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pupil dilation<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- relaxation of intestinal wall<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased cardiac activity<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Skin hair erection<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-074\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">74- Vasoconstriction of the blood vessels is due to stimulation of:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- α-adrenergic receptors in the blood vessels<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- β- adrenergic receptors in the blood vessels<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Nicotinic receptors in the blood vessels<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Muscarinic receptors in the blood vessels<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-075\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">75- Activation of alpha adrenergic receptors would:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increase rennin secretion from the kidney<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Constrict pulmonary arterioles<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Constrict bronchioles<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Dilate cerebral arterioles<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-076\" data-k=\"b\" data-alt=\"\" data-fx=\"حجب مستقبلات α بيقلّل المقاومة الطرفية وضغط الدم (الاختيار D)، وبيوسّع القصبات الهوائية شوية مش بيضيّقها. فالمفتاح المطبوع B (قطر القصبات) غالبًا غلط.\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">76- Blockade of α- adrenoceptors produces a decrease in:<span class=\"gtag warn\" dir=\"rtl\">مفتاح الملزمة مشكوك فيه<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Sweat production<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bronchus diameter<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Gastrointestinal motility<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Total peripheral resistance &amp; arterial blood pressure<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Heart rate<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-077\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">77- Norepinephrine will cause contraction of smooth muscles in the:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Bronchioles<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Pupils<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Intestines<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Arterioles<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Ciliary body<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-078\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">78- Increased release of epinephrine from adrenal medulla during muscular exercise:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Stimulates glycogenolysis in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Stimulates glycogenesis in the liver<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Causes vasoconstriction of arterioles all over the body<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Constricts the ciliary muscle in the eye<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-079\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">79- Stimulation of α- adrenergic receptors produce:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Hypotension<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Bronchodilation<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Lipolysis<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased cardiac contractility<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Mydriasis<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-080\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">80- About the chemical transmission in the sympathetic N.S:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Noradrenaline is released by both the pregang. &amp; postgang. Symp. nerve fibres.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Noradrenaline acts mainly on the beta adrenergic receptors.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Noradrenaline contributes to 80% of the secretion of the suprarenal medullae<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- The alpha adrenergic stimulators cause contraction of the plain muscles in the seminal vesicles &amp; vas deferens.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- The adrenal medulla secretes mainly at rest and during sleep.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-081\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">81- Drugs which stimulate α presynaptic receptors are used for treatment of hypertension because they produce:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Direct effect on blood vessels causing vasodilation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decreased heart rate<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Decreased secretion of noradrenaline from postganglionic sympathetic fibers<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Increased volume of urine<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-082\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">82- Which autonomic receptor mediates an increase in heart rate?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Adrenergic α receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Adrenergic β1 receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Adrenergic β2 receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Cholinergic muscarinic receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Cholinergic nicotinic receptors<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-083\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">83- When adrenergic receptors become activated:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Alpha1 receptors are stimulatory to heart rate<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Beta1 receptors are stimulatory to heart rate<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Beta2 receptors cause coronary vasoconstriction<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Beta1 causes lipolysis<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-084\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">84- Administration of a drug which inhibits norepinephrine synthesis is expected to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Cause bronchodilatation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Inhibit intestinal motility<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Decrease insulin secretion by pancreas<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Decrease the heart rate<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-085\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">85- Stimulation of β-receptors:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Decreases glucagon secretion by pancreatic β-cells<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decreases insulin secretion (M) by pancreatic β-cells<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Promotes glycogen synthesis in liver cells<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Promotes glycogen synthesis in muscle cells<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Promotes lipolysis<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-086\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">86- Farmers subjected to inhalation of insecticides containing irreversible anticholine esterase may present with all of the following, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Tachycardia<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Excessive salivation (A)<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- constriction of the pupils<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Bronchoconstriction<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-087\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">87- Cases of irreversible anticholinesterase intoxication can be treated by drugs that:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Block nicotinic receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Block muscarinic receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Stimulate nicotinic receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Stimulate muscarinic receptors<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-088\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">88- Adrenal medulla:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Receives preganglionic parasympathetic fibers<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Secretes 80% norepinephrine (H) and 20% epinephrine<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Is stimulated by acetylcholine<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Stimulation increases intestinal motility<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-089\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">89- Injection of drug that block muscarinic receptors produces the following except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Dryness of the mouth<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Inability to see near objects<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Decreased heart rate<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Decreased sweat secretion €<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-090\" data-k=\"a\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">90- Blockage of muscarinic receptors causes<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Loss of accommodation for near vision<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Constriction of the pupil (R)<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Constriction of the bronchi<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Diarrhea<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Micturition<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-091\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">91- If a patient is administered drug that block muscarinic receptors, one of the following is not expected to occur:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Dry tongue<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Excessive sweating<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Increased heart rate<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Inability to read a newspaper<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-092\" data-k=\"b\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">92- Administration of a muscarinic receptor antagonist leads to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increased sweat secretion<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Decreased sweat secretion<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Increased gastric motility<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Bronchoconstriction<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-093\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">93- The sympathetic nervous system has all of the following characters except<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- It is mostly noradrenergic.<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- It is involved more frequently in generalized actions.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- It is of little importance in visual accommodation.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- It antagonizes mostly parasympathetic functions.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- It is anabolic.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-094\" data-k=\"e\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">94- The parasympathetic nerves<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Are important in emergency conditions e.g. fight &amp; flight reactions .<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Play important functions in skin and skeletal muscles.<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Tend to have longer postgang . fibers than pregang. Fibres.<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Are catabolic in their actions.<\/li><li data-o=\"e\" tabindex=\"0\">e- Mostly exert effects opposite to those done by the sympathetic Nerves.<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-095\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">95- Administration of a drug which inhibits norepinephrine synthesis is expected to:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Cause bronchodilatation<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Inhibit intestinal motility<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Decrease insulin secretion by pancreas<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Decrease the heart rate<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-096\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">96- Sympatholytic drugs:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Inhibit adrenergic receptors but not beta receptors<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Inhibit norepinephrine reuptake by nerve terminals<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Inhibit enzymatic degradation of norepinephrine<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Block adrenergic receptors<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-097\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">97- Catecholamines, acting on the α-receptors, will produce:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Increase in heart rate<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Increase in contractility of atria<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Relaxation of wall of GIT<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-098\" data-k=\"c\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">98- Mono amine oxidase is important for:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Synthesis of acetylcholine<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Synthesis of noradrenaline<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Inactivation of noradrenaline in the liver<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-099\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">99- Which one of the following is wrongly paired?<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"a\" tabindex=\"0\">a- Pseudo choline esterase ------------plasma<\/li><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Monoamine oxidase ---------- inactivation of noradrenalin<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Edinger westephal nucleus --------------- reading a book<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Acetylcholine synthesis --------------- Acetyl CoAesterase<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><div class=\"gq\" data-id=\"ph2m-100\" data-k=\"d\"><p class=\"qt\" dir=\"ltr\">100- All about Acetylcholine is correct, except:<\/p><ul class=\"opts\" dir=\"ltr\"><li data-o=\"b\" tabindex=\"0\">b- Acts on the same type of receptor on postganglionic fibers in sympathetic and parasympathetic ganglia<\/li><li data-o=\"c\" tabindex=\"0\">c- Acts on the same type of receptor on target organs at cholinergic sympathetic and parasympathetic nerve terminals<\/li><li data-o=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\">d- Acts only as an excitatory neurotransmitter<\/li><\/ul><p class=\"res\" hidden><\/p><\/div><\/section><\/div><\/section><\/main>"}})(window.MG=window.MG||{});
